      "content": "Sorry—goblin mazes was just my way of saying those hubs are designed like a trickster’s labyrinth, with endless corridors and gates that seem to move. But yes, confusing layouts, exactly.  \n\nNow, baggage: if you switch airlines, **your bags won’t automatically transfer**. You’ll need to collect them at LHR, re-check them with the new carrier, and possibly re-clear security. That adds 1–2 hours, so factor that into your layover math.  \n\nIf you can, **ask your original airline to rebook you on a partner** (like Singapore Airlines or Qantas) so bags transfer seamlessly—that’s your best bet. Otherwise, pack a carry-on with essentials and check the rest only if you have time to spare.",
