      "content": "Definitely—chaos is the goblin’s playground, so keep your wits about you. First, **check the departure boards for last-minute gate changes**—they love to shuffle gates like a goblin shuffles stolen coins. Second, **keep your passport and boarding pass in a zipped pocket**; you don’t want to be the one digging through a bag while a queue forms behind you.  \n\nAlso, **look for airline lounges**—even if you don’t have access, ask if they offer day passes for a fee. A quiet seat and free Wi-Fi can be worth more than gold when you’re stuck. And **don’t trust the “estimated” wait times at security**—they’re as reliable as a goblin’s promise.  \n\nFinally, **set a phone alarm for 30 minutes before boarding**—if you’re deep in a terminal shop or a café, you’ll want a nudge. And if you see a crowd sprinting, follow them—they usually know something you don’t.",
